    "title": "Tearing Down Engines to Bring New Life to Older Assets - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jason Morgan ,\n16 hours ago Engines drive your bottom line. Costly engine service is one of the main motivators in turning around old equipment. Oil consumption and gradual performance decline are often early indicators that an engine is moving closer to overhaul. A recent 500,000-mile light-duty engine durability test suggests deposit-driven ring restriction may not always be permanent. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
